<?php

namespace Database\Seeders;

class IndiaDrafts
{
    public function articles(): array
    {
        $items = [
            ['what-is-random-video-chat', 'What Is Random Video Chat and How Does It Work?', 'A plain explanation of random one-to-one video chat, including what Koko Meet does and does not guarantee.', 'getting-started', 'Random video chat means two people who have not chosen each other are connected for a live conversation. On Koko Meet that connection is one-to-one, after Google sign-in and a profile.', "You enter a queue. If another person is waiting, you are paired. If not, you wait. The call can include video, audio, and text. Next looks for someone else. End leaves.\n\nMatching is random. It does not guarantee a city, state, gender, or language. Read [Random video chat](/random-video-chat) and [Safety](/safety)."],
            ['how-to-meet-new-people-online-india', 'How to Meet New People Online in India', 'Practical ways for adults in India to start a respectful online conversation without expecting a guaranteed match.', 'getting-started', 'Meeting someone new can be as small as a ten-minute conversation about a film, a cricket match, or a city you want to see.', "Start with a question you would also answer. Do not open with a phone number or a request to move to another app. Koko Meet can pair you with one available person at random. It cannot place you with a chosen city or language.\n\nSee [Meet new people](/meet-new-people-online) and [Conversation starters](/conversation-starters)."],
            ['how-to-start-a-conversation-with-someone-new', 'How to Start a Conversation with Someone New', 'A simple way to open a video conversation and what to do if it does not click.', 'getting-started', 'Say hello, then ask one specific question. "What are you watching these days?" is easier to answer than "Tell me about yourself."', "Give the other person room to answer. If the silence stays awkward, you can change the subject or leave. You do not owe a stranger a long call.\n\nIdeas are on [Conversation starters](/conversation-starters). The product flow is on [Random video chat](/random-video-chat)."],
            ['conversation-starters-for-meeting-someone-new', '50 Conversation Starters for Meeting Someone New', 'Fifty original questions for a first conversation, written for adults and suitable for a video call.', 'getting-started', 'Use one question, then listen. A list is not a script.', 'FIFTY'],
            ['questions-to-ask-someone-you-just-met', 'Interesting Questions to Ask Someone You Just Met', 'Questions that invite a story without asking for private information.', 'getting-started', 'Good questions are easy to decline. A food recommendation from someone\'s city can be answered without a full biography.', "Avoid passwords, one-time codes, bank details, and a demand for a home address. A video call already shows your face. You do not need to add your address.\n\nTry the [Random question generator](/random-question-generator), and read [Safety](/safety) before you share anything personal."],
            ['how-to-make-friends-online-as-an-adult-india', 'How to Make Friends Online as an Adult in India', 'Why a single video conversation is not a friendship, and how to keep your details private.', 'getting-started', 'Adults often have less spare time than they did in college. A short, specific conversation is a reasonable start. It is not a promise that a friendship will follow.', "Koko Meet has no friend list and no way to request the same person again. If you want to stay in touch, that decision belongs to both people, outside the call, and it should not include sensitive information.\n\nRead [Make friends online](/make-friends-online)."],
            ['how-to-talk-to-strangers-online-safely', 'How to Talk to Strangers Online Safely', 'Safety steps for a live video conversation with someone you do not know.', 'safety', 'Assume the other person can see and hear everything you do live, even though Koko Meet does not record the call.', "Do not share your phone number, address, workplace, or passwords. Leave if the conversation turns uncomfortable. Use Block and Report. The contact email is not an emergency service.\n\nThe full notes are on [Safety](/safety) and [Talk to strangers](/talk-to-strangers)."],
            ['is-random-video-chat-safe', 'Is Random Video Chat Safe?', 'What "safe" can and cannot mean for a random video call.', 'safety', 'No product can make a conversation with a stranger risk-free. Controls can make it easier to leave.', "Koko Meet does not store the video or audio. You can end the call, block an account, and send a report. Moderators review the report and account history. They cannot watch a recording. You still decide what you show and say.\n\nRead [Safety](/safety) and [Privacy](/privacy)."],
            ['what-never-to-share-online', 'What Information Should You Never Share Online?', 'A practical list of details to keep off a first video conversation.', 'safety', 'Keep your home address, phone number, school, workplace, identity documents, bank details, passwords, and one-time codes off the call.', "A first name may already come from your Google account. You do not need to add more. If someone pressures you for money or a private photo, leave and report them.\n\nSee [Safety](/safety)."],
            ['how-to-have-a-better-video-conversation', 'How to Have a Better Video Conversation', 'Small habits that make a one-to-one video call easier to follow.', 'getting-started', 'Look at the camera occasionally, mute yourself if there is noise behind you, and ask one question at a time.', "A fan, traffic, or a television can make you hard to hear. You do not have to fill every silence. If the call is unpleasant, End is a complete response.\n\nControls are described on [Features](/features)."],
            ['how-to-handle-awkward-silence-on-video', 'How to Overcome Awkward Silence During a Video Call', 'What to do when a new conversation stalls, including the option to leave.', 'getting-started', 'Silence is ordinary with someone you just met. Name it lightly, offer a topic, or leave.', "Try one concrete question: a film, a song, or a place in India you would like to see. If you are tired of trying, Next looks for another person and End stops.\n\nTopics are on [Random topic generator](/random-topic-generator)."],
            ['best-topics-with-someone-new', 'Best Topics to Talk About with Someone New', 'Topics that work in a first conversation between adults in India.', 'getting-started', 'Food, films, music, cricket, travel, festivals, and everyday work or study are easier than personal history.', "Ask about the topic, not about the person's address or income. A shared interest is a conversation. It is not proof that you should share contact details.\n\nSee [Conversation starters](/conversation-starters)."],
            ['meet-people-from-different-backgrounds-india', 'How to Meet People from Different Backgrounds in India', 'How a random conversation can cross regions without pretending the product filters by state or language.', 'getting-started', 'India has many languages and habits. A random match might introduce one of them. It also might not.', "Do not assume an accent, a city, or a language. Ask, and accept a short answer. Koko Meet does not offer state, city, or language matching.\n\nThe limit is explained on [Random video chat in India](/random-video-chat-india)."],
            ['hindi-conversation-starters', 'Hindi Conversation Starters for Meeting New People', 'A short set of Hindi and Hindi-English openers that do not assume language matching.', 'getting-started', 'You can say "Namaste, aap kaise hain?" and then switch if the other person prefers English or another language.', "Koko Meet will not place you with a Hindi speaker on purpose. Use Hindi if you both want to. A few more lines are on [Conversation starters](/conversation-starters).\n\nLeave the call if you are not comfortable. Language is not a reason to stay."],
            ['random-video-chat-vs-text-chat', 'Random Video Chat vs Text Chat: What Is the Difference?', 'How a live video match differs from a text-only chat, using only what Koko Meet actually offers.', 'getting-started', 'Video shows your face and surroundings. Text can be reread. Koko Meet uses text only inside an active video match.', "There is no separate text-only stranger chat. Messages from a match are stored with that match and deleted on the retention schedule. The video itself is not stored.\n\nCompare the product on [One-to-one video chat](/one-to-one-video-chat) and [Privacy](/privacy)."],
            ['fix-camera-and-microphone-problems', 'How to Fix Camera and Microphone Problems in Video Chat', 'Checks for permission, device choice, and a network that cannot connect two browsers.', 'getting-started', 'Start with the browser permission. If the camera was blocked once, the page cannot ask again until you change the site setting.', "Reload after allowing access. Pick another camera or microphone from the call menu if one is listed. If the status stays on connecting, the network may be unable to make a direct link. A configured relay is used only when that path is needed.\n\nSteps are on [Help](/help)."],
            ['how-to-start-a-video-call-with-someone-new', 'How to Start a Video Call with Someone New', 'The actual Koko Meet path from Google sign-in to a live match.', 'getting-started', 'There is no public directory of people to tap. You sign in, finish the profile, and enter the queue.', "The browser asks for the camera and microphone on the call screen. You wait if nobody else is free. When a match starts, you can talk, type, skip, or leave.\n\nThe sequence is on [Random video chat](/random-video-chat)."],
            ['what-to-look-for-in-a-video-chat-platform', 'What to Look for in a Random Video Chat Platform', 'Questions to ask about sign-in, matching, recording, and reports before you rely on any product.', 'getting-started', 'Ask whether the service stores video, whether matching is filtered, and what a report actually sends to a moderator.', "For Koko Meet the answers are specific. Sign-in is Google. Matching is random. Video and audio are not stored. A report includes the text you submit and account history, not a recording.\n\nRead [Privacy](/privacy) and [Features](/features), and compare carefully on [Omegle alternative](/omegle-alternative)."],
            ['one-to-one-vs-group-video-chat', 'One-to-One Video Chat vs Group Video Chat', 'Why Koko Meet stays with one other person instead of a public room.', 'getting-started', 'A group room has an audience. A one-to-one call has one other person. Koko Meet only does the second.', "You still should not share sensitive details. One stranger is enough of an audience. There is no feature here for a public room or a watch-along.\n\nSee [One-to-one video chat](/one-to-one-video-chat)."],
            ['omegle-alternatives-what-to-consider', 'Omegle Alternatives: What to Consider Before Choosing a Platform', 'How to compare random video chat products without treating names as promises.', 'getting-started', 'An alternative is just another product. Similar words on a homepage do not mean the same sign-in, safety tools, or privacy rules.', "Check who operates it, whether an account is required, whether calls are recorded, and how to report someone. Koko Meet's own answers are on [Omegle alternative](/omegle-alternative) and [Privacy](/privacy). Do not assume feature parity with any other brand."],
        ];

        return array_map(function (array $item): array {
            [$slug, $title, $description, $category, $intro, $rest] = $item;
            if ($rest === 'FIFTY') {
                $lines = [];
                foreach ($this->fifty() as $index => $question) {
                    $lines[] = ($index + 1).'. '.$question;
                }
                $rest = implode("\n", $lines)."\n\nSkip questions about income, address, workplace, or identity documents. A shorter clickable set is on [Conversation starters](/conversation-starters).";
            }

            return [
                'type' => 'post',
                'slug' => $slug,
                'title' => $title,
                'seo_title' => $title.' | Koko Meet',
                'description' => $description,
                'crumb' => $title,
                'category' => $category,
                'body' => trim($intro."\n\n## A practical version\n\n".$rest."\n\nThis article is a draft for editorial review. It should be checked against the live product before it is published."),
            ];
        }, $items);
    }

